WEBVTT

00:00:05.042 --> 00:00:06.550
Welcome to Stewardship.

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:14.614
This is a place to learn how to build redemptive technology, practise what you learn, and bring your questions to a mentor.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:19.794
We are following a demonstration participant through a real learning programme.

00:00:26.927 --> 00:00:30.337
The curriculum adapts FaithTech’s four D cycle.

00:00:30.337 --> 00:00:34.182
Discover begins with the people carrying the problem.

00:00:34.182 --> 00:00:37.592
Discern invites God’s wisdom into the response.

00:00:37.592 --> 00:00:40.857
Develop turns discernment into faithful work.

00:00:40.857 --> 00:00:45.211
Demonstrate shares the impact and what the team has learned.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:47.823
A preparation module opens the path.

00:01:02.773 --> 00:01:06.998
This participant has two sections completed as starting fixtures.

00:01:06.998 --> 00:01:09.208
Continue resumes the next reading.

00:01:09.208 --> 00:01:14.084
Each module includes an assignment and questions for a mentor conversation.

00:01:14.084 --> 00:01:19.804
Learning here connects what you read with what you do and the questions you still carry.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:38.115
The completed sections have been saved, and reloading preserved our place.

00:01:38.115 --> 00:01:40.551
Finishing Prepare unlocked Discover.

00:01:40.551 --> 00:01:45.083
The path reflects the work this participant has actually completed.

00:01:45.083 --> 00:01:49.276
Earlier reading stays available when you need to return to it.

00:02:01.679 --> 00:02:08.293
Before moving on, we have saved a reflection about listening to the people affected by a problem.

00:02:08.293 --> 00:02:11.498
The complete note remains here after reloading.

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:17.431
It belongs to its module, so the context can travel with us into our next conversation.

00:02:33.265 --> 00:02:37.694
Our mentor’s published availability gives us a choice of times.

00:02:37.694 --> 00:02:39.873
Taken slots cannot be selected.

00:02:39.873 --> 00:02:45.426
We have booked an open time, and the learning path shows the same conversation.

00:02:45.426 --> 00:02:50.207
The mentor, time zone, and remaining session allowance help us plan.

00:03:00.143 --> 00:03:02.557
Preparation begins before the meeting.

00:03:02.557 --> 00:03:08.973
We have answered a prompt from the current module, and the saved answer appears beneath the question.

00:03:08.973 --> 00:03:16.659
A specific reflection gives the conversation somewhere useful to begin, while leaving room for what we have not resolved.

00:03:21.597 --> 00:03:27.508
We have switched to a separately prepared advanced participant to review Develop.

00:03:27.508 --> 00:03:31.594
Their earlier learning was seeded before this recording.

00:03:31.594 --> 00:03:38.527
Inside Develop, FaithTech’s co-creation cycle is Request, Receive, Review, Render, and Rejoice.

00:03:38.527 --> 00:03:41.373
These movements repeat around the work.

00:03:45.095 --> 00:03:50.386
Request names the actual work in prayer and invites the Holy Spirit into it.

00:03:50.386 --> 00:03:52.405
Receive makes room to listen.

00:03:52.405 --> 00:03:56.512
The team records what comes without rushing to evaluate it.

00:03:56.512 --> 00:04:00.132
Listening is given time before a solution is chosen.

00:04:03.073 --> 00:04:07.504
Review brings those observations together and weighs them as a team.

00:04:07.504 --> 00:04:10.827
Render puts the supported next steps into practice.

00:04:10.827 --> 00:04:14.802
Careful design, testing, and honest engineering still matter.

00:04:14.802 --> 00:04:21.904
The aim is to build from shared discernment, with a clear connection between what was heard and what is done.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:27.911
Rejoice closes the iteration with specific thanks.

00:04:27.911 --> 00:04:34.511
It gives the team time to name what was received and learned, before the next task takes over.

00:04:34.511 --> 00:04:36.477
Then the cycle begins again.

00:04:36.477 --> 00:04:44.201
This curriculum draws on FaithTech’s Playbook and Workbook; it is an adaptation, without implying endorsement.

00:04:56.026 --> 00:05:01.388
Back with our original participant, the same programme works on a narrow screen.

00:05:01.388 --> 00:05:06.750
The menu keeps the learning path, reflections, and mentor sessions within reach.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:11.308
Your preparation can continue wherever you have a few quiet minutes.

00:05:14.398 --> 00:05:18.845
We have signed out, and protected pages now require a new sign-in.

00:05:18.845 --> 00:05:30.030
Stewardship brings reading, practice, reflection, and mentorship into one place, helping participants take their next faithful step in building redemptive technology.

